# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTHING PERSONAL GOES TO GITHUB
#
# This repo is PUBLIC. The apps export real data — what Tom ate, weighed,
# slept, lifted and spent, and video of clients — and none of that belongs
# on a public remote. These rules keep every file the apps produce out of
# git, so the only way to publish personal data is to go out of your way.
#
# Source files are named after what they are (skins.json, launch.json), so
# none of the patterns below can catch one. There is deliberately no blanket
# *.json rule for that reason.
#
# If you have something personal that these do not match, put it in
# private/ — that whole folder is ignored.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# backups the apps write: motherbase-status-2026-08-21.json, motherbase-all-*.json
motherbase-*.json
motherbase-*.xlsx
*-backup.json
*.backup.json

# the older LifeOS exports
lifeos-*.json

# spreadsheet exports — readable copies of the whole log
*.xlsx
*.csv

# pictures the apps generate from real data
# STATUS share cards (status-S-96-story.png) and FORM snapshots
status-[A-F]-*.png
status-S-*.png
formreview-*.png

# client video, and anything dropped in to review
*.mp4
*.mov
*.m4v
*.webm

# screenshots of real logs
Fitnotes Screen Shots/
*Screen Shots/
*Screenshots/

# anything you want kept off the remote, no questions asked
private/

# ─── ordinary build and editor noise ───
node_modules/
*.log
.check.js
block.prev.html
.claude/settings.local.json
